      "note": "The whole house from the K16 kit (T-1909), refined from the district draft in place under the draft's id. READ from the 1911 sheet 35 raster at full size (0.186 m a pixel), carried into the draft's lot plan frame through the T-1250 fit (the same fit the trace s35fp-2000-b2 stands on): the main body 17.1 m deep and 7.3 m along Prairie (columns 589-681, rows 285-325); the front block 6.4 m deep and 5.5 m along the street (to column 715.5), marked '3BB'; beside it on the north the two-storey range the sheet marks '2' (rows 283.5-293.5), 1.9 m wide; the one-storey porch marked '1' across the front, 1.76 m deep (to column 725); on the north flank a canted bay 6 m across at the wall and 1.4 m out; on the south flank a room 5.6 m across and 1.5 m out ending in a canted bay 1.5 m deeper; and behind it the canted two-storey room marked '2BB', 5.6 m across and 3.8 m out. RECONSTRUCTED and recorded as L-k16-2000-2010-frame-1909: no picture of the house is known, so everything the plan does not fix is the kit's and the reconstruction rules' — the 1.0 m raised basement, storeys of 3.3, 3.1 and 2.9 m, every opening (cased two-over-two sash, three to five to a storey on the long flanks, the door on the front under the porch), the bracketed eave, the 25-degree hips and the flat decks of the lower ranges, the canted bays carried the full height of the part they stand on, the one brick stack and the body's paint. The porch's return along the front block's south side (rows 323-334: the kit's porch runs one wall) and the narrow brick (pink) range on the rear wall, 0.75 m deep, whose height the sheet does not print, are not built."
