  "research_note": "T-1909 refines the district draft (T-2351) in place under the same id: the whole house is rebuilt from the K16 timber kit — clapboard walls, cased sash, a bracketed eave under low hips, canted bays and a porch across the front — on the outline the 1911 Sanborn sheet 35 draws (s35fp-2000-b2, register row frontage-35-059). No photograph, print or drawing of the house has been found in the Prairie library or data/sources/; its elevations are a bounded reconstruction (liberty L-k16-2000-2010-frame-1909). The register reads 2010 as similar to 2000 and the sheet draws them alike; they are given different paint, porch depths and side ranges where the sheet differs, never one facade repeated.",
